I think it's a bug according to the mysql 5.7 document, and it's fixed in mysql 8.0:
```sql
MySQL(root@localhost:test) > drop table t;
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.11 sec)

MySQL(root@localhost:test) > create table t(a char(2) primary key, b char(2));
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.06 sec)

MySQL(root@localhost:test) > insert into t values("a ", "b ");
Query OK, 1 row affected (0.03 sec)

MySQL(root@localhost:test) > set @@sql_mode="PAD_CHAR_TO_FULL_LENGTH";
Query OK, 0 rows affected (0.01 sec)

MySQL(root@localhost:test) > select * from t where a = "a";
Empty set (0.00 sec)

MySQL(root@localhost:test) > select version();
+-----------+
| version() |
+-----------+
| 8.0.11    |
+-----------+
1 row in set (0.00 sec)
```

